# OpenCode Bar environment template.
#
# The app itself needs no configuration file to run: on Windows it stores
# settings in %APPDATA%\opencode-bar\config.json and encrypts the API key with
# DPAPI. This file exists so a contributor (or an agent) knows every
# environment variable the project reads.
#
# Copy to `.env` only as a local reference. `.env` is NOT read by the app - do
# not wire up a dotenv loader, and never commit `.env`; the one real variable
# below can be set in your shell or in the IDE run configuration instead.

# OpenCode Go API key. Overrides the DPAPI-protected key stored in config.json
# when set, which is how you run the app against a live account without
# touching the stored secret. Create one in the OpenCode console
# (https://opencode.ai/console).
#
# The value carries the key prefix shown in the app's paste prompt. Treat it as a
# live credential: it grants access to your Go plan usage data.
# Do not commit it, echo it, or paste it into an issue, a log or a test fixture.
OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=

# Everything else lives in config.json, not in the environment. For reference,
# the defaults the app writes on first run:
#
#   pollMinutes  = 5
#   thresholds   = [75, 90, 100]
#   notifyPools  = ["go"]
#   trayPool     = "go"
#   apiBase      = "https://opencode.ai"   # the only host the app contacts
#
# See README "Configuration" for the full table and AGENTS.md for the privacy
# invariants.
